	Section:
		Text: Pages and breaks
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Page numbers
		Paragraph: In any text, `{page}` writes the number of the page and `{pages}` the last number of the count. The footer of this document is a `Page overlay` with both, so each of its three pages carries its own number.
			Style: intro
		Text: Text: Page {{page}} of {{pages}}
			Style: label
		Paragraph: The footer at the bottom of this page says "Page 1 of 3". The next two pages are forced with `Before: page`.
		Block:
			Style: marked
			Break:
				Before: page
			Paragraph: The second page. Its footer says "Page 2 of 3".
		Block:
			Style: marked
			Break:
				Before: page
			Paragraph: The third and last page. Its footer says "Page 3 of 3".
